codex
I’m choosing a direct two-loop implementation that counts even elements across both inputs and compares that count with `len(lst1)`. This gives a clean full-domain invariant: after each loop, the accumulator equals the initial accumulator plus the even-count of the consumed suffix. The implementation does not mutate either input list.
apply patch
patch: completed
/workspace/solution.py
diff --git a/solution.py b/solution.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..be99ca1d4ddf899ff799ab36d044be8c2132ad2c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/solution.py
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+def exchange(lst1, lst2):
+    """Return whether exchanges can make every element of lst1 even."""
+    even_count = 0
+    for value in lst1:
+        if value % 2 == 0:
+            even_count += 1
+    for value in lst2:
+        if value % 2 == 0:
+            even_count += 1
+    if even_count >= len(lst1):
+        return "YES"
+    return "NO"

