Rather than assuming the prover can refine a three-way numeric disjunction into a static sort, I’m making the induction explicit: separate empty, Int-head, Bool-head, and Float-head loop claims, each with an arbitrary numeric tail. Those four mutually recursive claims cover heterogeneous lists of every finite length; the entry theorem remains a single unbounded claim.
